  "review_notes": [
    "διὰ παντός taken as noncompositional under rule 45: 'always' is a single English word answering to neither the preposition nor the quantifier separately. Splitting it — a bare 'always' on παντός with the preposition unrepresented under rule 34 — remains defensible, but the corpus glosses πᾶς 'all' and never 'always', so no part of the word answers to the token alone."
